    "summary": "Extended Java wire fixture generator and offline Rust test suite to cover Fetch advertised version boundaries: v4 classic (oldest spoken, topic names, untagged replicaId, partition errors, omitted logStartOffset), v5 (logStartOffset gate on follower replica request and response), v7 (session metadata gate with sessionId, sessionEpoch, forgotten topics, and aborted transactions list), v11 (classic format boundary before flexible, rackId, preferredReadReplica, realistic record batches with records before requested offset and ABORT/COMMIT marker sequences), v12 (first flexible version, compact encoding, clusterId, DivergingEpoch, CurrentLeader, SnapshotId, and unknown tagged fields), v13 (topic IDs wire transition replacing topic names), v15 (replica-field transition omitting untagged replicaId and adding replicaState tagged field 1), v16 (nodeEndpoints tagged field 0 in response), and v17 (highest 3.9.1 valid version, partition replicaDirectoryId tagged field 0). Tests distinguish a valid short final fetch tail from malformed complete records. Mutation tests verify required version gates and field order."
